---
title: "Who owns each close-outcome alias step?"
accTitle: "Bob versus Mac ownership for x and s aliases"
accDescr: "Mac Capture routes x and s into capture-rewrite. Bob swaps and lexes. Mac applies the edit with native undo and restores a literal letter on a second press of the same key. bob capture keeps typed xx, and capture-parse sees the rewritten close."
config:
  flowchart:
    rankSpacing: 12
    nodeSpacing: 16
    wrappingWidth: 240
---
flowchart TD
  KEY["`**Mac routes x and s**<br/>rewrite lane`"]
  RW["`**Bob capture-rewrite**<br/>swap and lex`"]
  APPLY["`**Mac applies the edit**<br/>native undo`"]
  ARM["`**Second same key**<br/>restores the letter`"]
  PARSE["`**capture-parse**<br/>sees x! and x*`"]
  CLI["`**bob capture**<br/>keeps typed xx`"]
  KEY ==> RW
  RW ==> APPLY
  APPLY --> ARM
  APPLY --> PARSE
  CLI -.->|"pasted or CLI draft"| PARSE
  class KEY,APPLY,ARM focus
  class RW,PARSE outcome
  class CLI muted
  classDef focus fill:#E8F1FB,stroke:#3B78C2,stroke-width:1.5px,color:#0F2E52
  classDef outcome fill:#E7F5EC,stroke:#2E7D4F,stroke-width:1.5px,color:#123D24
  classDef muted fill:#F3F4F6,stroke:#6B7280,stroke-width:1.5px,color:#1F2937
